@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #fcfcfd
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam arrowColor #0f172a
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #fff7d6
skinparam noteBorderColor #b45309
skinparam noteFontColor #334155
skinparam roundcorner 16
title Activity - distributeddatabase/DistributedDatabase
skinparam activity {
  backgroundColor #f8fafc
  borderColor #0f172a
  fontColor #0f172a
  diamondBackgroundColor #e2e8f0
  diamondBorderColor #1d4ed8
  diamondFontColor #0f172a
  startColor #1d4ed8
  endColor #0f172a
  barColor #1d4ed8
}
start
partition "Observe and Bind" {
:Start from shared flow\nshared/diagrams/shared-reconcile-activity.svg;
:Read desired DistributedDatabase spec, tracked\nstatus, and delete intent;
if ("Tracked or explicit OCI identity present?") then (yes)
:Get the current OCI resource via\nGetDistributedDatabase;
else (no)
:Resolve an existing OCI resource through\nListDistributedDatabases using filters\ncompartmentId, displayName, dbDeploymentType,\nlifecycleState;
:Create the OCI resource via\nCreateDistributedDatabase when no reusable\nmatch is found;
:Persist the resolved or created OCI identity\ninto status;
endif
}
if ("Delete requested?") then (yes)
partition "Delete" {
:Delete path uses DeleteDistributedDatabase\nwith required via GetDistributedDatabase or\nListDistributedDatabases to DELETED, NOT_FOUND\nconfirmation;
:Confirm deletion via GetDistributedDatabase or\nListDistributedDatabases until OCI reaches\nDELETED, NOT_FOUND;
if ("Delete cleanup and finalizer release succeed?") then (yes)
:Remove the finalizer after delete completion;
else (no)
:Stay blocked until cleanup or finalizer\nrelease succeeds;
endif
}
stop
else (no)
partition "Lifecycle Classification" {
if ("OCI state in retryable set?") then (yes)
:Request requeue while OCI remains in CREATING,\nUPDATING, DELETING;
stop
endif
if ("OCI state is outside success targets?") then (yes)
:Return an unsuccessful reconcile result until\nOCI reaches ACTIVE, INACTIVE;
stop
endif
}
partition "Ready and Drift Handling" {
:Compare live OCI state against the\nrepo-authored mutation surface;
if ("Force-new or conflicting drift detected?") then (yes)
:Reject drift before OCI mutation for force-new\nfields compartmentId;
stop
endif
if ("Supported mutable drift detected?") then (yes)
:Apply UpdateDistributedDatabase only for\nmutable fields definedTags, displayName,\nfreeformTags;
else (no)
:Skip the no-op mutation path;
endif
:Run provider helper hooks\ncreate=tfresource.CreateResource;\nupdate=tfresource.UpdateResource;\ndelete=tfresource.DeleteResource when the\nmatching field-driven path executes;
:Apply explicit follow-up semantics\ncreate=read-after-write;\nupdate=read-after-write; delete=confirm-delete;
:Return success for the ACTIVE, INACTIVE\nsuccess state;
:Project required status and finalizer policy\nretain-until-confirmed-delete;
:Requeue on provisioning, updating, terminating;
}
endif
stop
note right
shared diagram:
shared/diagrams/shared-reconcile-activity.svg
Start from the shared reconcile activity and
specialize provider-backed CRUD, wait, and
status-projection details here.
Controller-local activity diagrams add
list-lookup hints, secret policies, delete
handling, and open formal gaps.
archetype batch: Generated service-manager
controllers specialize the shared reconcile path
with formal runtime ownership.
service: distributeddatabase
slug: distributeddatabase
kind: DistributedDatabase
archetype: generated-service-manager
status/finalizer: required /
retain-until-confirmed-delete
requeue: provisioning, updating, terminating
provider states: create CREATING; update
UPDATING; delete DELETING
follow-up: create=read-after-write;
update=read-after-write; delete=confirm-delete
supported drift: definedTags, displayName,
freeformTags
reject before mutate: force-new fields
compartmentId
create-only fields: none
list lookup:
oci_globally_distributed_database_sharded_databases
filters compartmentId, displayName,
dbDeploymentType, lifecycleState; exact
compartmentId plus displayName list filters
preserve dbDeploymentType and lifecycleState
when already known, then narrow summary
candidates in memory to a unique exact prefix
plus dbDeploymentType match
conflicts: none
open gaps: none
Create-body normalization keeps shard and
catalog `source` inputs compatible with the OCI
SDK: CRD `EXISTING_CLUSTER` values serialize as
the SDK's `EXADB_XS`, scaffold-only `jsonData`
is dropped, and explicit false booleans in
nested vm-cluster and backup-config payloads are
preserved.
Reviewed lifecycle mapping treats CREATING as
provisioning, UPDATING as updating, ACTIVE and
INACTIVE as success, NEEDS_ATTENTION and FAILED
as terminal non-success, and DELETING as
terminating.
ListDistributedDatabases returns
DistributedDatabaseSummary items that omit
fields such as scanListenerPort,
latestGsmImageDetails, shardDetails,
catalogDetails, gsmDetails, dbBackupConfig, and
gsmSshPublicKey, so every successful bind or
write path rereads GetDistributedDatabase before
projecting steady-state status.
The provider resource exposes broader patch,
state-transition, and trigger update families,
but the current CRD does not publish those
controls; the package-local runtime only
performs in-place updates through
UpdateDistributedDatabaseDetails for
displayName, freeformTags, and definedTags.
Delete keeps the finalizer until
GetDistributedDatabase or list fallback confirms
DELETED or NOT_FOUND.
end note
@enduml
